schema: "0.4"
id: npl-brutalist-40-mock-mcp-builder
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — Mock MCP Builder: generates a mock MCP server from a prose
# description for testing agent integrations without hitting production tools.
# Theme tenets: three-band builder, zero radius, load-bearing hard borders, flat
# electric accents, hard-offset block shadow as the only depth.
# Palette: vermilion #ff2d00, ultramarine #1500ff, hazard-yellow #ffe600,
# white #ffffff, black #000000, surface-alt #f2f2f2.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a builder /
    tooling surface inside a developer console, in a NEO-BRUTALIST register: raw structure
    shown as the machinery it assembles. Flat fills only — no gradient, glow, blur, or
    soft shadow; the only depth cue is a hard-offset SOLID block shadow with zero blur.
    Geometric grotesk (Space Grotesk) UPPERCASE 700 for titles and tool names; Space Mono
    for descriptors, schema, and inputs. No serif. Zero corner radius. Borders are
    load-bearing, always at full strength.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the MOCK MCP BUILDER screen of NoizuPromptLingo — a
    builder that generates a mock MCP server from a prose description, for testing agent
    integrations without hitting production tools — rendered as raw, structural machinery.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands on a pure white canvas, separated by 2px solid black rules,
    aligned to a hard grid): a left PROSE DESCRIPTION INPUT, a center GENERATED TOOL LIST,
    and a right TOOL DEFINITION EDITOR, with a header bar on top.

    HEADER BAR: an uppercase grotesk 700 title "MOCK MCP BUILDER", a mono breadcrumb slug
    (like "/mock-mcp/shipping-api"), and a solid vermilion "PUBLISH MOCK SERVER" button —
    rectangular, 2px black border, black uppercase mono label, hard-offset black block
    shadow with zero blur.

    LEFT PROSE DESCRIPTION INPUT: a large hard-bordered textarea, zero radius, no inner
    shadow, an uppercase mono label "DESCRIBE THE SERVER" above it, filled with a few lines
    of plain-language description (e.g. "A shipping API with tools to create shipments,
    track parcels, and fetch rates"). A bordered "GENERATE TOOLS" button beneath it with a
    hard-offset shadow.

    CENTER GENERATED TOOL LIST PREVIEW: a vertical stack of hard-bordered rectangular tool
    rows butted together, separated by 1px black rules, zero radius — each row an uppercase
    grotesk tool name (e.g. CREATE_SHIPMENT, TRACK_PARCEL, FETCH_RATES) with a one-line mono
    descriptor and a small mono parameter count. The selected row is a full inverted block
    (solid black, white text) with a thick vermilion accent bar on its left edge.

    RIGHT TOOL DEFINITION EDITOR: a hard-bordered panel, header separated by a full-weight
    rule, showing the selected tool's schema as an editable mono block on a light-gray
    surface — field rows (NAME, TYPE, REQUIRED, DESCRIPTION) with bordered mono inputs, zero
    radius. A pure-ultramarine focus outline sits on the currently-edited field. A
    hazard-yellow "UNSAVED" tag (solid yellow, black text, black border) in the header.

    PALETTE & TYPE: pure white canvas, pure black ink and full-strength borders, electric
    vermilion for the publish button and the selected accent bar, hazard yellow for the
    unsaved tag, pure ultramarine for focus — flat and whole at maximum saturation. Space
    Grotesk uppercase for titles and tool names, Space Mono for descriptors, schema, and
    inputs. No serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero radius on every input, row, and panel; 1-2px solid black borders
    at full strength; the only depth is a hard-offset solid block shadow (zero blur) on the
    publish and generate buttons and the schema block. No gradient, glow, blur, or soft
    shadow.

    MOOD: raw, structural, high-voltage — a builder that shows the machinery it assembles.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, rounded corners, drop-shadow blur, soft shadow, gradient, neon glow, pastel colors, frosted glass"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the builder — header with Publish, left prose description textarea + Generate Tools, center generated tool list preview, right tool definition schema editor"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Brutalist language — zero radius, full-strength solid black borders, flat vermilion accent + hazard-yellow unsaved tag + ultramarine focus, hard-offset block shadow (zero blur) as only depth, Space Grotesk uppercase tool names + Space Mono schema, no serif, no gradient/glow/soft shadow"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear three-band builder flow (prose -> tools -> schema) on a hard grid, clear selection, plausible real tooling UI"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible mono schema, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "rounded corners, soft/blurred drop shadow, gradient, glow, or frosted glass present"

tags: [npl-brutalist, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, mock-mcp, builder]
